  "name": "polish batch: same-state update no-op, escapeAttr rename, read-error mapping, new-dir parent fsync, coverage tooling, lock-test margin",
  "slug": "polish-batch-same-state-update-no-op-escapeattr-rename-read",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Low-severity cleanups gathered from the audit; each is small and independent.",
    "details_md": "1) update --state <same> is a fake mutation (bumps updated_at, emits empty ticket.updated) — short-circuit like E1 did for draft/undraft. 2) html.ts escapeAttr is a misleading alias for escapeHtml with no scheme validation — rename or fold in real URL validation. 3) readEntityFile only maps ENOENT; wrap non-ENOENT (EACCES/EIO) in a SlopError naming the path. 4) atomicWriteFile fsyncs a newly-created dir but not its parent — fsync each new dir’s parent for full durability. 5) add @vitest/coverage-v8 + a CI threshold so untested code is flagged. 6) lock.test.ts renewal-timing test has a thin real-time margin (20ms vs 80ms) — widen or use a fake clock.",
    "acceptance": [
      "Each of the six items is either fixed or explicitly deferred with a note"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/tickets/update.ts:141,166-167",
      "src/web/html.ts:29-32",
